From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 21 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: zones for more than two duelists (no Extra Monster Zone
 mirror, per duelist disabled zones)

Zone work for n_duelists > 2. With 2 duelists every stock statement stays as it was.

Changed sites: the Extra Monster Zone mirror in refresh_location_info_instant and in RefreshLoc step 7
(2 sites, guarded with n_duelists == 2); the mirror check in is_location_useable (1 site);
the opponent part of get_linked_zone and get_linked_cards (2 sites); the four places that split an
EFFECT_DISABLE_FIELD value in two halves for players 0 and 1 (2 in the instant refresh and RefreshLoc step 0,
1 in RefreshLoc step 2; all with n_duelists == 2 keeping the stock text); the message at the end of both
refreshes (2 sites); Duel.CheckTiming and Duel.IsEnvironment (2 functions, loops over the living duelists).

New behaviour for n > 2: every duelist has its own 2 Extra Monster Zones, nothing is mirrored or swapped.
An EFFECT_DISABLE_FIELD value is relative to its handler: low 16 bits = own zones, high 16 bits = the next
duelist in turn order. EFFECT_BECOME_LINKED_ZONE uses the same split. The new message MSG_FIELD_DISABLED_N (202)
replaces MSG_FIELD_DISABLED: u8 count, then count x (u8 duelist, u32 own disabled zones in the low 16 bits).
It is sent when the zones of any duelist change. The ids 200, 201 and 202 are added to common.h together.
RefreshLoc gets one member (previously_disabled_n) for the old zones of every duelist.

With 2 duelists nothing changes: the stock text is inside n_duelists == 2 branches, the loops in CheckTiming
and IsEnvironment visit duelist 0 then 1 in the same order with the same result (nobody is eliminated).
Left for other tasks: the card.cpp and libcard zone code that still uses opponent_of (phase 3 fold).

